          ],
          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/render-kg-to-cdn.svg",
          "description": "Render a Knowledge Graph — the whole of it, or a list of its Subgraphs — for publication to a CDN at a publication root URL, and report a STATUS and a MESSAGE. Owner, 2026-09-30: \"render content of a KG (or list of subgraphs within) for publication to a CDN at a given publication root URL … independent of staging vs publication … just rendering … output is status of push to CDN + message\".\n\nSTAGING AND RELEASE ARE THE SAME PROCESS. A preview is this with a root under the release root; a release is this with the release root. What differs — who may start it, what is verified first, what else on the host must survive the push — belongs to the CALLER: `feature-staging` and `docs-site-publish` call this and keep their own steps around the call.\n\nTOOL-AGNOSTIC ON PURPOSE. Owner, 2026-09-30: \"tools can describe their own specific subprocesses if needed to not bog down general skills\". The one call activity names the skill; the Tool for the chosen target satisfies it and lists its own `subprocesses`, which is what the call descends into. For GitHub Pages that is the `gh-pages` Tool and bootstrap-tools' render-kg-to-github-pages. No step here is GitHub's.",
          "enforcement": "strict",
          "flowCount": 8,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
          "name": "Render a Knowledge Graph to a CDN",
          "nodeCount": 8,
          "sourcePath": "processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn",
          "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/blob/main/cat-harness/processes/process/render-kg-to-cdn.bpmn",
          "startNode": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_RenderKgToCdn/node/Start_Render",
          "summary": "Render a Knowledge Graph — the whole of it, or a list of its Subgraphs — for publication to a CDN at a publication root URL, and report a STATUS and a MESSAGE."
        },
