        {
          "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_DocsSite",
          "@type": "bootstrap:Process",
          "conformsTo": [
            "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#externalSchema/omg-bpmn-2.0",
            "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#externalSchema/omg-dd-1.0"
          ],
          "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/assets/img/workflows/docs-site-publish.svg",
          "description": "Publish the docs site to `gh-pages`, verify the export before the deploy, and keep the open pull requests' previews alive across a deploy that replaces the whole branch. PUBLISHING THE SITE IS A FULL REPLACE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS IS DRAWN. Bean `7yvd`. The workflow is 432 lines and its shape is not legible from them: what a reader needs to know is that `gh-pages` is REPLACED wholesale, so anything on that branch which this build did not produce is gone unless something puts it back.\n\nThat is bean `plj1` — every open pull request's review preview deleted by an unrelated merge, silently, for months. The repair is the two steps either side of the publish, and they are a PAIR: `Restore the open PRs' staging previews` copies them into the publish directory before the replace, and `Did the previews survive?` reads the deployed ref afterwards. Neither is sufficient alone — a restore nobody verifies is a restore that can silently stop working, which is exactly how the original defect lasted.\n\nBOTH GATEWAYS REFUSE RATHER THAN WARN, and the second is three-state: it fails on a preview that is missing AND on a check that could not tell, because a verification that has gone blind must not read as permission. Same rule as `ci-health` — could-not-determine is never rendered as clean.\n\n`Regenerate every derived reference from its source` stands for five separate generators (schema reference, skill instruction pages, content-backed docs, the translation index, the BPMN renders). They are drawn as one task on purpose: they are independent of each other and sequential only because a single job runs them, so five boxes would assert an ordering the workflow does not have.\n\nMechanical throughout. There is no human lane, which is what makes `build-pipeline` the right lane rather than a convenient one. VERIFIED AND ALERTED (bean vigi, owner 2026-09-23): the export is verified BEFORE the deploy and blocks it on anything but a pass; and every step after the publish button that fails — an incomplete export, a verification failure, a failed deploy, a lost preview — goes through one alert to the publication manager. A clean publish closes that alert.",
          "enforcement": "strict",
          "flowCount": 17,
          "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
          "name": "Publishing the docs site, and keeping the previews alive",
          "nodeCount": 15,
          "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/docs-site-publish.bpmn",
          "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/blob/main/cat-harness/processes/sdlc/docs-site-publish.bpmn",
          "startNode": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#process/Process_DocsSite/node/Start_Push",
          "summary": "Publish the docs site to `gh-pages`, verify the export before the deploy, and keep the open pull requests' previews alive across a deploy that replaces the whole branch."
        },
